{"packet_id":"D007-01","doc_id":"D007","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"AB 12 security deposit cap and return rules","requirement":"Landlords may charge only one month's rent as a security deposit, though qualifying small landlords may charge two months. Deposits must be returned within 21 days with an itemized statement of deductions.","key_value":"1 month's rent; 2 months for qualifying small landlords","coverage_conditions":"Landlords generally; landlords owning only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total may charge up to two months' rent.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"landlords who own only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total, held by a natural person, family trust, or LLC whose members are all natural persons","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":"Photograph requirement applies to tenancies that begin on or after July 1, 2025.","coverage_quotes":["Starting July 1, 2024, many landlords may only charge one month's rent for unfurnished and furnished units","Starting July 1, 2024, landlords who own only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total can charge up to two months' rent for furnished and unfurnished units if ownership is held by a natural person, family trust, or limited liability company (LLC) where all members are natural persons"]},"exemptions":"Landlords who own only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total, held by a natural person, family trust, or LLC of natural persons, may charge up to two months' rent.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-07-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"AB 12","quoted_span":"Starting July 1, 2024, many landlords may only charge one month's rent for unfurnished and furnished units","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D007-01","doc_id":"D007","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance security deposit interest","requirement":"Landlords of units covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance must pay tenants interest on security deposits at the end of each year and a prorated amount if the tenant moves out before the end of the year.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"other","text":"units fully or partially covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance"}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["For tenancies in units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance, landlords must pay tenants interest on their security deposit at the end of each year and a prorated amount if the tenant moves out before the end of the year."]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.76","quoted_span":"For tenancies in units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance, landlords must pay tenants interest on their security deposit at the end of each year and a prorated amount if the tenant moves out before the end of the year.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
